items: v3-host-io-bytes
paths: file:v3/src/Exec.scala file:v3/src/Lower.scala
scope: |
  SSC3-12 slice B. `readFile`/`writeFile` as a COMPOSITION of prims, because v2's `io.readFile`
  gives BytesV and `std/fs.ssc` declares a String:

      readFile(p)      ->  utf8->str(io.readFile(p))
      writeFile(p, s)  ->  io.writeFile(p, str->utf8(s))

  The IR is SHARED, so `Exec` must implement all four, which needs v3 to hold a byte string — it
  has no value for one. So this adds `Value.VBytes`.

  THE HAZARD IS NAMED BEFORE THE CODE: a new `Value` case does NOT fail to compile at the matches
  that need it, because most end in a catch-all. The slice includes an audit of every `Value` match
  rather than trusting the compiler.

  NARROW: two files. No std, no board, no gate script. `v3/tests/front/` gains a fixture, additive.
